As Janis suggested, try your experiments in debug mode.
Start the game with "nethack.exe -u wizard -D" There's a
list of extended commands available through "?". If you want
a set of starting items for each new game so you don't have
to wish for a dozen things each time, create a list in a
text file, name it wizkit.txt and save it in the directory
with nethack.exe.

Now just ^g and specify a tame whatever. You may even be
able to get pets you can't get in the game.

Having a powerful pet in the very early game will
consistently present some very difficult problems. As you
noted, the bones files are awful. You can become separated
and the pet can go feral. The pet can kill peaceful humans
that are much more useful to you alive. Pets that eat will
snatch things you need for intrinsics. An early, powerful
pet lets you get deeper in the dungeon than you could get
that early in the game on your own and then if you get
separated or the pet is busy eating it can't save you.
